      <h2>Building lives from <em>the inside out.</em></h2>
      <p>Alongside her husband, Pastor Godman Akinlabi, Pastor Bola Akinlabi serves as Global Co-Lead Pastor of The Elevation Church. The church began in a hall on Lagos Island in 2010 and has grown into a global church family with expressions across Africa, Europe, America and beyond.</p>
      <p>She brings her own gifts to building the church. Her strategic approach to leadership has helped shape key areas of church life, from the children’s ministry to the administration, people and financial structures that support the church’s growth.</p>
      <p>Her ministry brings biblical teaching and practical wisdom together, with a particular heart for women, children and families.</p>

      <h2>Faith, structure <em>and stewardship.</em></h2>
      <p>Before giving herself fully to ministry, Pastor Bola spent years in treasury and financial management. That work gave her a gift for structure, order and stewardship, and it is the foundation for how she serves today: building the church with care, clarity and integrity.</p>
      <p>She holds a Bachelor’s degree in Economics from Ahmadu Bello University, Zaria, an MBA from the University of Lagos (Unilag), and a Postgraduate Diploma in Financial Strategy from the University of Oxford. She is also a Certified John Maxwell Leadership Trainer.</p>
      <blockquote class="pull">“Her worth is made up of so much more than the physical attributes that define her.”<cite>Pastor Bola on why Made for More exists, ThisDay, 2018</cite></blockquote>

      <h2>A ministry for <em>women.</em></h2>
      <p>Pastor Bola is the visionary behind Jewels, the women’s ministry of The Elevation Church, and the convener of the annual Made for More Conference. Since 2015 it has grown from a gathering in Lagos into a movement with editions in London and Toronto, helping thousands of women discover purpose and embrace their calling.</p>

      <h2>Mentoring &amp; <em>coaching.</em></h2>
      <p>A Certified John Maxwell Leadership Trainer, she speaks at conferences and mentors women and emerging leaders, creatively weaving biblical stories into her coaching.</p>
      <p>Through one-to-one and group mentoring, she invests in women and leaders to discover their purpose, grow in confidence and build lasting impact.</p>
      <div class="btn-row mt-3"><a class="link" href="/speaking/">Invite Pastor Bola {{ arrow() }}</a></div>

      <h2>Family <em>first.</em></h2>
      <p>Among all her accomplishments, Pastor Bola counts her family as her greatest calling. She is the wife of Pastor Godman Akinlabi and the proud mother of two daughters.</p>
      <div class="btn-row mt-4"><a class="btn" href="/speaking/">Invite Pastor Bola {{ arrow() }}</a><a class="link" href="/press-kit/">Download the press kit {{ arrow() }}</a></div>
